# A level load that hangs is reported as a hang with its stack (#440): the hang watchdog's threshold lowered to
# 1 s, the next level load stalled for 3 s right after its "Loading level" line (the channel's 'stall load'), then
# 'loadlevel 1'. The watchdog must report the main thread stalled in the load - the stalling function by name, the
# load under it - before the load goes on, then the main thread responsive again; the level loads.
@args --loadlevel 10

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s

watchdog 1000
stall load 3000
loadlevel 1
@log Loading level "graph/levels/level1/level1.dlf" 10s
@log \[hang\] main thread stalled for \d+ ms \(report 1 of at most 3\), last beat at level load 10s
@log \[hang\]   #\d+ arx\.exe\+0x[0-9a-f]+ platform::stallThisThread 10s
@log \[hang\]   #\d+ arx\.exe\+0x[0-9a-f]+ .*(notifyLoading|loadLevel|DanaeLoadLevel|ARX_CHANGELEVEL) 10s
@log \[hang\] main thread responsive again after \d+ ms 10s
@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@assert area eq 1
